You are a senior review consolidator. Multiple independent reviewers have scored the same generated code.
Synthesize their feedback into a single consensus review.

## Original Prompt

Create a TypeScript Node.js project that provides a reusable Azure Blob Storage management utility.

The project needs:

- A **service class** that wraps blob operations: upload (with optional metadata and blob index tags for later querying), download, list blobs in a container, and delete. The upload method should handle large files efficiently using streaming — uploading a multi-gigabyte file should not load the entire thing into memory. The service should also prevent concurrent writers from overwriting each other's changes when updating the same blob by acquiring a lease before writing.

- A **configuration module** that connects to Azure securely using the storage account endpoint (from an environment variable). No connection strings or account keys should be used — the app will run in Azure with managed identity. The configuration should set up a custom retry policy (exponential backoff, configurable max retries and delay) and enable SDK logging at a configurable level for debugging.

- A **main script** that wires everything together and demos each operation: uploads a sample file with some index tags, lists all blobs in the container, downloads the file back and prints its content, acquires a lease and overwrites the blob, then finally deletes it. Print status at each step.

Include a complete `package.json` with the necessary Azure SDK dependencies and a `tsconfig.json`.

## Individual Reviews

### Reviewer 1 (claude-opus-4.6)
```json
{
  "model": "claude-opus-4.6",
  "scores": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "name": "Code Builds",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Code structure is sound: correct imports, proper TypeScript types, valid tsconfig.json. Lock file resolves all dependencies. @azure/logger is available as transitive dep of @azure/storage-blob. Unable to run tsc due to environment restrictions but no obvious compilation issues."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Lock file resolves @azure/storage-blob@12.31.0 (latest) and @azure/identity@4.13.1 (latest). TypeScript 5.9.3 and @types/node 22.19.17 are current."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential, streaming uploads, proper async/await, retry configuration, lease-based concurrency control, and clean separation of concerns across modules."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No RestError-specific error handling anywhere. No catch blocks for 409 lease conflicts or 404 not-found scenarios. Only a generic top-level catch in main.ts. The uploadWithLease method lets 409 errors propagate as untyped exceptions."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Well-structured with clear separation (config, service, main). Good JSDoc comments, consistent naming, proper use of TypeScript types and interfaces. Clean demo flow in main.ts."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All Azure SDK dependencies use @azure/ scoped packages: @azure/identity, @azure/storage-blob, @azure/logger. No deprecated unscoped packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential from @azure/identity. No hardcoded connection strings, account keys, or SAS tokens. Reads endpoint from environment variable."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "BlobServiceClient constructed with endpoint URL and credential object: new BlobServiceClient(accountUrl, credential, { retryOptions }). No connection string patterns."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All asynchronous operations use async/await. No .then()/.catch() chains. Entry point uses top-level async function with .catch() for unhandled errors."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses for-await-of over listBlobsFlat() which is correct, BUT the listBlobs() method collects ALL results into an array (blobs.push(blob)) before returning — violating the requirement to not accumulate all pages in memory."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "No long-running operations exist in blob storage upload/download/delete/list scenarios. This criterion is not applicable and no incorrect manual polling is used."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No RestError import or catch anywhere in the codebase. No statusCode inspection for error-specific handling. All errors propagate as generic exceptions."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All dependencies are current @azure/* track packages. No deprecated azure-storage, azure-arm-*, ms-rest-azure, or @azure/ms-rest-* packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses setLogLevel() from @azure/logger and configures AzureLogger.log for custom output. Supports both programmatic config and AZURE_LOG_LEVEL environment variable."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Valid package.json with @azure/identity and @azure/storage-blob. Includes tsconfig.json, @types/node, and TypeScript 5.x. Minor note: @azure/logger is imported directly but only available as transitive dependency — works but not ideal."
      },
      {
        "name": "Configures custom retry policy via StorageRetryOptions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses StorageRetryOptions with StorageRetryPolicyType.EXPONENTIAL, configurable maxTries, retryDelayInMs, and maxRetryDelayInMs. Passed to BlobServiceClient constructor."
      },
      {
        "name": "Enables SDK logging via @azure/logger setLogLevel()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Calls setLogLevel() from @azure/logger with configurable level. Also supports AZURE_LOG_LEVEL environment variable fallback."
      },
      {
        "name": "Implements blob lease acquisition before overwrite using BlobLeaseClient",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "uploadWithLease() acquires lease via BlobLeaseClient.acquireLease(), uploads with lease condition in options, and releases lease in finally block."
      },
      {
        "name": "Uses BlockBlobClient.uploadStream() for large file streaming upload",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both upload() and uploadWithLease() use blockBlobClient.uploadStream() with fs.createReadStream(), 4MB buffer size, and concurrency of 4. Does not buffer entire file."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets blob index tags on upload via tags property",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "UploadOptions includes tags property which is passed to BlockBlobUploadStreamOptions.tags. Demo sets tags: { environment: 'dev', project: 'blob-manager' }."
      },
      {
        "name": "Downloads blob and reads response via readableStreamBody",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "download() method accesses response.readableStreamBody and pipes through streamToString() helper that reads chunks from the Node.js Readable stream."
      },
      {
        "name": "Lists blobs using for await...of async iteration over listBlobsFlat()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses for await (const blob of this.containerClient.listBlobsFlat()) pattern for async iteration."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles lease conflict errors (409 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No catch block for 409 status code on lease acquisition. The acquireLease() call in uploadWithLease() will throw on conflict but no RestError handling or 409-specific logic exists."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles blob not found errors (404 status code) on download/delete",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "download() has no 404 error handling — will throw generic error if blob doesn't exist. delete() uses deleteIfExists() which avoids 404 but download() is unprotected."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using uploadData() or upload() with full buffer",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Correctly uses uploadStream() with fs.createReadStream() in both upload methods. No uploadData() or upload() with Buffer."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using connection strings or account keys",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential with endpoint URL from environment variable. No connection strings, account keys, or SAS tokens anywhere."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT collecting all listed blobs into an array before processing",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "listBlobs() collects all blobs into an array via blobs.push(blob) before returning the complete array. This is the exact anti-pattern the criterion warns against."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 21,
